 "readme_markdown": "# Run 1: Base meme coin PAPER trading, 2026-11-18 23:20 ET to 2026-11-22 23:21 ET\n\nPaper trading only. No wallet, no real money. Archived on 2026-11-22 at about 23:22 ET by user order: archive run 1 and restart fresh under the new rules.\n\n## Money\n- Start: $100 active bankroll (bankroll #1) plus a $900 untouched reserve, for a $1,000 total budget. Total deposited into the active book was $100, with no refills.\n- Final equity: **$74.1164** cash with 0 open positions after the reset close, plus the $900 reserve = $974.12 against the $1,000 budget (**-$25.88**, -25.9% on the active $100).\n- Realized P&L: -$25.8836 across 101 closed trades: **20 wins, 81 losses**.\n- Best trade: #97 VDINO, +$3.005 (+79.3%). Worst: #1 CHUBBY, -$7.00 (-100%, LP rug).\n\n## Reset close\n- #95 VVVCAT (Private Cat, contract 0xb200...8502) was entered 2026-11-22 13:24 ET at $3.74.\n- It was closed at about 23:22 ET as a RESET CLOSE at the last recorded price, 5.250e-05 minus 1% slip: **-$0.0741 (-1.98%)**, held 9h57m.\n- **FLAG:** the price had not changed since 13:25:16 ET, so it may be untradeable or frozen. A real exit may not have been possible.\n- `status.json` in this folder was written by the watcher at 23:21, before the reset close, so it still lists #95 as open. `ledger.json` is the final record.\n\n## winner_pattern (the only setup traded from Nov 20 02:25 ET)\n- 12 closed (#90-#101 plus the #95 reset close): **4 wins / 8 losses, +$0.6786**. Average win +44.21%, average loss -19.32%.\n- Excluding the #95 reset close: 11 trades, 4W/7L, +$0.7526.\n- Wins:\n  - #92 AX1 +30.96%\n  - #94 PI +39.29%\n  - #96 VVVCAT +27.31%\n  - #97 VDINO +79.28%\n- Losses:\n  - #90 AX1 -15.1%\n  - #91 XDP -2.0%\n  - #93 AX1 -13.9%\n  - #98 VDINO -35.9%\n  - #99 FAN -61.0%\n  - #100 AUTO -18.7%\n  - #101 VDINO -6.0%\n  - #95 VVVCAT -1.98% (reset close)\n- Before winner_pattern (Nov 18-20), the other setups went 6W/69L for -$29.14 (per the Nov 20 switch note).\n\n## Key lessons (full text per trade is in ledger.json `mistake`/`lesson` and the xlsx Mistakes & Lessons sheet)\n1. **Fresh launches under ~$25k liquidity rug.** An LP pull jumps past any stop (#1, #2, #21, #32, #37, #42, #43).\n2. **Stops gap on thin pools.** The real loss is the next printed price, not -10%: #90 -15%, #93 -14%, #98 -36%, #99 -61%, #100 -19%.\n3. **Same ticker does not mean the same coin.** AX1 (3 contracts), VDINO (3 contracts in 4h20m) and VVVCAT (2 contracts) were copycat relaunches. Re-entering a ticker right after a take-profit lost every time (#93, #98).\n4. **A logged lesson does nothing until it is coded.** The #93 re-entry lesson (Nov 20) was never coded, and #98 repeated it.\n5. **Operations matter.** The 10 MB xlsx was rewritten every watcher cycle, so checks happened about every 20s instead of 12s, with 21 stale-heartbeat watcher kills on Nov 22. The scout held the ledger lock for 261s on the 22:44 round, which left #100 unwatched for about 4.5 min.\n6. **Upside gaps happened too.** #97's +79% was a price jump past the target, not a repeatable edge.\n7. **Winner study (Nov 22, n=11, in-sample).** All 4 winners had 5m +50..+185%, vol1h/liq >= 0.82, liq >= $26k, buys/sells >= 2.0 and no recent take-profit on the same ticker. Score, 1h change, entry hour, source and honeypot status did not separate winners from losers.\n\n## Rule history (see trades.md for timestamps and full notes)\n- **Nov 18 23:20:** starting filters (sells exist, honeypot check, liq/FDV checks, momentum). Tight, mid and wide test plans.\n- **Nov 19:** many fresh_launch penalties (thin-liq rugs, static pools, one-sided flow). after_style setup (#16 After) added. Dead-pool and thin-flow passes. Re-entry only near the prior peak. 45-min flat time stop.\n- **Nov 20 02:25:** USER switched to trading ONLY winner_pattern (fresh <6h, 1h >= +100%, vol1h/liq >= 0.6, buys >= 2x sells, buys >= 25, liq >= $10k, 5m > 0). Plan: SL -10%, TP +25%, 8% trail arming at +15%. Size 10% of equity (5% if the token is not indexed on honeypot.is).\n- **Nov 21 18:57:** supervisor.py runs round.py every 5 min (the scout had silently stopped for about 9h). The 5m > 0 rule was coded.\n- **Nov 22 23:09:** filters coded. (a) No same symbol/address entry for 2h after a take-profit win. (b) winner_pattern score >= 12. (c) liq >= $20k. autolesson.py auto-fills a mistake and lesson for every close.\n- **Nov 22 23:16-23:20 (USER):** six-factor gate F1-F5, F6 time stop, TP +20% full sell, breakeven stop at +10%, pre-buy re-quote, continuous scanning, 3s watcher, 5% sizing, $500 equity halt. These are the run 2 rules, effective from the run 2 start.\n\n## Backtest of the run-2 rules on #90-#101 (in-sample, observed ~12-20s ticks; see code/backtest_v2.py)\n- The gate passes #90, #92, #94, #96 and #97. It blocks #91, #93, #98, #99, #100 and #101. No winner is blocked.\n- The new exits changed nothing on the observed ticks: winners still filled at the first price above +20%.\n- Results: actual +$0.7526. Gate plus new exits +$6.0409 (5 trades, 4W/1L). If wins fill exactly at +20% (more likely with 3s checks), **+$2.2361**.\n\n## Files\n- `ledger.json`: final run-1 ledger.\n- `paper_trading_journal.xlsx`: full journal including the 79k-row Scout Log sheet.\n- `scout_log_run1.csv`: Scout Log exported from the xlsx.\n- `trades.md`: run notes.\n- `live_feed.log` and `live_feed.log.1`: every TICK, BUY, EXIT and SCOUT line.\n- `status.json`, `scout_latest.json`, `scout_loop.log`, `watcher.err`.\n- `code/`: round.py, watcher.py, supervisor.py, autolesson.py as of the archive, plus the backtest script.\n- Note: one more old-code scout round (23:22:51-23:23:26 ET, 0 buys, from an outside keepalive restart) ran after this archive was copied. It is in the live /home/box/memecoin-paper/scout_loop.log, not in this folder's copy.\n",
 "note": "Run 1 used a $100 active bankroll plus a $900 untouched reserve and older rules (trailing stops, +25% TP). Six-factor gate checks did not exist yet, so checks are null."
